steps:
EDIT 1 (required) — `/workspace/src/theme/dark.ts` lines 56-63. Replace the `matrixAxis` helper so it also carries a dark divider colour, and use the semantic token name instead of the raw ramp step.
CURRENT (verbatim, unique in file):
```ts
const matrixAxis = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.neutral20
    }
};
```
REPLACEMENT:
```ts
const matrixAxis = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.borderTint
    },
    dividerLineStyle: {
        color: color.border
    }
};
const matrixBody = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.borderTint
    }
};
const matrixCorner = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    }
};
```
Notes: `color` is `tokens.darkColor` (`src/theme/dark.ts:22`). `color.borderTint === color.neutral20` in the dark ramp (both resolve to `rgba(40,43,48,1)`), so this line is a rename with zero visual change — it just mirrors the light default `tokens.color.borderTint` at `MatrixModel.ts:229`. `color.border` (= dark `neutral30` = `rgba(65,67,72,1)`) mirrors the light default `tokens.color.border` at `MatrixModel.ts:239`. `matrixCorner` deliberately does NOT set `itemStyle.borderColor`, because the light default for corners is `'none'` (`MatrixModel.ts:229`, `isCorner ? 'none' : ...`) and theme values win over defaults — setting one would give dark mode corner borders that light mode does not have.

EDIT 2 (required) — `/workspace/src/theme/dark.ts` lines 187-196. Replace the whole `matrix` theme block: rename the bogus `backgroundColor` key to the real `backgroundStyle`, delete the dead `innerBackgroundStyle` key, wire up `body`/`corner`, and replace the two hard-coded hexes with tokens (every other entry in this file uses tokens).
CURRENT (verbatim, unique in file):
```ts
    matrix: {
        x: matrixAxis,
        y: matrixAxis,
        backgroundColor: {
            borderColor: '#817f91'
        },
        innerBackgroundStyle: {
            borderColor: '#484753'
        }
    },
```
REPLACEMENT:
```ts
    matrix: {
        x: matrixAxis,
        y: matrixAxis,
        body: matrixBody,
        corner: matrixCorner,
        backgroundStyle: {
            borderColor: color.axisLine
        }
    },
```
Effect of each key: `backgroundStyle.borderColor` → dark `axisLine` = dark `neutral70` = `rgba(165,166,171,1)`, a light grey outer border on the dark `rgba(2,5,11,1)` canvas — the exact inverse of the light theme's dark `#54555a` border on `#f4f7fd`, and it replaces the previously-inherited light-theme `#54555a` that was invisible on dark. `x/y.dividerLineStyle.color` → dark `border`, replacing the inherited light `#b7b9be`. `body.itemStyle.borderColor` → dark `borderTint`, replacing the inherited light `#cfd2d7` (this is the 'light-theme border colors leaking through' in the acceptance signal). `body.label.color` / `corner.label.color` → dark `secondary` (dark `neutral70`, light grey) replacing the inherited light `secondary` `#54555a`, which was near-black text on a near-black cell.

EDIT 3 (recommended) — add a regression unit test at NEW file `/workspace/test/ut/spec/coord/matrix/darkMode.test.ts`. The directory `test/ut/spec/coord/` does not exist yet but is already matched by `'**/spec/coord/**/*.test.ts'` in `/workspace/test/ut/jest.config.cjs:52`. Start the file with the standard 18-line Apache licence header (copy it verbatim from the top of `/workspace/src/theme/dark.ts`) — `npm run lint` enforces it. Body:
```ts
import { createChart, getECModel } from '../../../core/utHelper';
import { EChartsType } from '../../../../../src/echarts';
import tokens from '../../../../../src/visual/tokens';

describe('coord/matrix/darkMode', function () {
    let chart: EChartsType;
    afterEach(function () { chart && chart.dispose(); });

    it('dark theme should override every matrix colour default', function () {
        chart = createChart({ theme: 'dark' });
        chart.setOption({
            matrix: { x: { data: ['a', 'b'] }, y: { data: ['c', 'd'] } }
        });
        const m = getECModel(chart).getComponent('matrix') as any;
        const dark = tokens.darkColor;
        expect(m.get(['backgroundStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(dark.axisLine);
        expect(m.get(['x', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(dark.borderTint);
        expect(m.get(['y', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(dark.borderTint);
        expect(m.get(['x', 'dividerLineStyle', 'color'])).toEqual(dark.border);
        expect(m.get(['y', 'dividerLineStyle', 'color'])).toEqual(dark.border);
        expect(m.get(['body', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(dark.borderTint);
        expect(m.get(['body', 'label', 'color'])).toEqual(dark.secondary);
        expect(m.get(['corner', 'label', 'color'])).toEqual(dark.secondary);
        // no light-theme token may leak through
        [['backgroundStyle', 'borderColor'], ['x', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'],
         ['x', 'dividerLineStyle', 'color'], ['body', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'],
         ['body', 'label', 'color']].forEach(function (path) {
            expect([tokens.color.axisLine, tokens.color.borderTint,
                    tokens.color.border, tokens.color.secondary])
                .not.toContain(m.get(path as any));
        });
        // corner keeps its borderless look in dark mode too
        expect(m.get(['corner', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual('none');
    });

    it('light (default) theme is unchanged', function () {
        chart = createChart();
        chart.setOption({ matrix: { x: { data: ['a'] }, y: { data: ['b'] } } });
        const m = getECModel(chart).getComponent('matrix') as any;
        expect(m.get(['backgroundStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(tokens.color.axisLine);
        expect(m.get(['body', 'itemStyle', 'borderColor'])).toEqual(tokens.color.borderTint);
        expect(m.get(['x', 'dividerLineStyle', 'color'])).toEqual(tokens.color.border);
    });
});
```
API notes verified against the repo: `createChart({theme})` is `/workspace/test/ut/core/utHelper.ts:33-59` (it forwards `theme` to `init`), `getECModel` is at `:141`, and `registerTheme('dark', darkTheme)` is at `/workspace/src/core/echarts.ts:3288`. `utHelper` imports `src/echarts.all`, so the matrix component (`/workspace/src/component/matrix/install.ts`) is registered. `ts-jest` runs with `diagnostics: false` (`jest.config.cjs:39`), so the `as any` casts on the path arguments are only for editor ergonomics.
